error[ffi_unknown_tag]: `fixedbugs-145-types.h` has no `struct anon_u` — clang read the header, and the struct it cannot lay out is an empty one C made up at this line
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-145-a-typedef-of-an-anonymous-union-is-not-a-tag.hero:16:18
     |
  16 |     record U tag anon_u partial  #~ ffi_unknown_tag
     |                  ^^^^^^
  note: `anon_u` is the name of a typedef in the header, and no struct carries that tag: a record takes a typedef by its own name, with no `tag`, `record anon_u partial` (§ 13)

error[ffi_parameter_type]: `p` of `use_anon_u` is declared a different kind of thing from the header's `anon_u *` — clang read the header, and the two do not convert
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-145-a-typedef-of-an-anonymous-union-is-not-a-tag.hero:18:5
     |
  18 |     function use_anon_u(@p: U) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: §4.19: a parameter is declared as what the header says. `anon_u *` has no name in this language — if it is a struct, declare it as a `record` inside this same `extern` group and the header owns its layout
